Loading a process's image leaves the core's count of the entries it turned on as it was,
so a load after it turns off none of them, and a process with fewer regions than the one before
keeps the other's regions past its own.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: PMP CSRs grant rights the slots do not

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -38,7 +38,6 @@
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
     pmp_load(process_pmp_addr(proc), process_pmp_cfg(proc), proc->pmp_count, core->pmp_loaded);
-    core->pmp_loaded = proc->pmp_count;
 }
 
